I hereby invite the Demigod(ess) bar to a fashionshow. All the latest in 
draconic scales have been brought in from Yendor.

Well, yes. After I wished up my GDSM, every dragon and its grandmother 
dropped scales, including a couple of my steeds. So I brought along one 
of each colour. :)

I find the knight a bit hard at the very beginning, but I've learnt that 
until I find a key/lockpick or am at least level 5, the pony is a 
sidekick and very good thief (lots of apples for training), but not yet 
steed. The chance of falling and hurting myself badly is too high. 
Excalibur is dipped for, and I trained up to twoweapon with the lance. I 
found lots of enchant weapon, and 3 magic lamps by the time I'd gotten 
to minetown (2 - one each of cursed and blessed at Izchac's (sp?)) So I 
got my armour fast. Kept a spare lamp, and one lightsource. My first was 
also my last, it's still at inventory letter O where it started, now 
blessed for emergency wishing.

I can't remember much of the game, no notes and took me a week or two 
from start to finish. 


I do remember ID'ing /oTurn Undead the lucky way.  My first dragon steed
had just died in the big room, I find an unknown wand 10 steps away, and
zap it at the corpse. Blackbird I shook off the dust and went on living.
He later went through a stage of Sasquatch before becoming Yellowstone
the Yellow Dragon. (Lived up to his name when he happily ate a
cockatrice corpse, I'd forgotten he was stoning resistant) Then a black
dragon was generated in my stashroom in the castle and disintegrated
both grey steed and yellow partner. And saddle.  I wished up a new one
and tamed the black. Rodney turned up and I /oDeathed him which bounced
back on my dragon. Not even a corpse left?!?  I finally found the saddle
in my inventory, seconds before using up my last lamp to wish for that
too. Used a wand wish for a blessed figurine of a new dragon. I see
praises for Ki-rin, but they seem to have no resistances whatsoever. So
I stick to Black or Silver D.

Black Beauty II stayed with me to ascension, though he made good work on
my /oTU on the Astral.

As I mentioned here on rgrn earlier, I found a bonesfile in Asmodeus' 
lair, with both Foobrands, and the Longbow which I had to leave. I found 
the hefty part of that bones later on an Ogre (+4 GDSM, +5 Helm of 
Telepathy, Gauntlets of Power, etc). On the next level were small 
critters with heavy weapons - Vorpal Blade and Mjollnir. I saw someone 
with Sunsword on Astral, but didn't take the time to get it.

The mysterious force wasn't half bad for a lawful, and the planes were 
fairly easy. Used up a wand of teleport and a bit of /oPolymorph on Air, 
Water took ages, Fire was very close. Used a crystal ball for all 
planes. Rodney gave me an encore on Earth.

Astral made heavy use of charm monster and had to recharge the /oTU 
once. Death to the right guarded Neutral, Pestilence in the middle for 
Lawful. I brought a [HoOA, but it sort of feels better not to have used 
it. I was also happy when I'd ditched the crystal ball and quaffed 2 
full healings, and was finally unburdened against Pestilence. Luckily 
dragons don't die from illness, so having P occasionally hit Black 
Beauty II was a real relief.

Anyway. Here's the dump.

Fashionshow tonight. :)

